# Relativity first-principles research design

2026-10-03. Combined research team; separate [special relativity](special-relativity.md) and [general relativity](general-relativity.md) frameworks, with SR built first. This is owner-authorized prose research, not a production plan, item acceptance, run transition, readiness receipt or publication request. Only this relativity research directory is owned. No plan-spec, production items/pages, engines, imports or mathematical originals were edited.

The proposal contains 27 A pages and 27 B leaf companions. Reserved A budgets range from16 to78 and B budgets8–12, below the100-item cap. These are closure budgets, not assertions that every reserved item has been proved. Exact prerequisites and scope limits are in [mathematics-audit.md](mathematics-audit.md) and [mathematical-prerequisites.md](mathematical-prerequisites.md); actual research-only acyclicity, resolution, B-leaf and budget checks are in [proposed-inventory-and-checks.json](proposed-inventory-and-checks.json), and direct supplier byte checks are in [supplier-byte-check.json](supplier-byte-check.json).

## Ordered architecture and claims

SR01→SR02→SR03/04 establishes adopted affine Minkowski spacetime, units, postulates, transformations, clocks and observer measurements. SR05–07 and SR08 then develop conditional causality/clock/light and momentum claims. SR09–11 address explicit matter/force assumptions, accelerated charts and controlled Newtonian correspondence. SR12 reserves empirical interface development without invented experiments. GR01–04 rebuild geometry/tensors/connection/geodesic/curvature suppliers under distinct Lorentzian-manifold hypotheses. GR05 adopts Einstein plus chosen matter dynamics. GR06 makes local balance and qualified global charges explicit. GR07 supplies explicit flat/Newtonian bridge claims. GR08–10 provide restricted spherical, cosmological and weak-wave models. GR11 gives causal definitions/examples/focusing, GR13–15 provide completed global geometry/PDE/MGHD arguments; GR12 has a primary-report research queue.

Within each A page, definitions and mathematical prerequisites precede physical assumptions needed to formulate a model; conditional deductions follow. Mathematics has mathematical premises only. In schema supplier→consumer notation, mathematical definitions→postulates are formulation prerequisites; postulates→physical theorems/thought experiments are physical assumptions; earlier deductions→later deductions are physical results. Experiment analysis mathematics is procedural/operational support, never a deduction of observed outcomes. Actual empirical premises must carry reported conditions and uncertainty through every consumer. Empirical support/testing links remain relations outside the DAG. B pages are leaves and cannot supply another page. Nothing depends forward on an OPEN result or a recorded-unproved remark.

Flat SR and metric GR are not silently identified: local tangent Minkowski structure is not a global inertial chart, and flat GR vacuum requires Λ=0/T=0 or another explicitly consistent source. Newtonian correspondences state quantity maps, small parameters, domains, derivative bounds and matter scaling. There is no universal GR global conserved energy, no generic global tetrad or Cauchy surface, no conflation of coordinates with observer congruences, and no quantum-gravity reconciliation.

